        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=\\sin{\\left(x \\right)},$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}{\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}\\,\\text{d}x &= 8\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ &= 8\\ln|u|+C \\\\ &= 8\\ln|\\sin{\\left(x \\right)}|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
